-- Step 38: commission earned on invoices, released as the customer pays, taken back on a
-- return or a bounce, approved and paid.
-- track: C
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- What a plan gives on a line is Step 37's (app.commission_on_line, app.commission_managers).
-- This step says when, and keeps the account of it:
--
--   An invoice is posted      each salesperson on each line earns what their plan gives on their
--                             share of the line, and each manager above them the team rate of
--                             their own plan on the same share. One accrual each, and one journal:
--                               debit   Sales commission (expense)
--                               credit  Commission payable
--   The customer pays         as much of each accrual is released as of the invoice has been
--                             collected. Cash and bank money count when the receipt is posted,
--                             a cheque when it clears. No journal: it is the same liability.
--   A cheque bounces after    the release goes back. If the commission had been paid by then,
--   it cleared, or a receipt  the person owes it back: it is taken out of what they are paid
--   is cancelled              next, and carried forward until it is all back.
--   Goods come back           what is earned comes down in the proportion of the goods, with
--                               debit   Commission payable
--                               credit  Sales commission (expense)
--                             and the return comes off the seller's sales for the month it is
--                             dated in, which a plan's slabs and target are measured on.
--   Approval                  the owner or an accountant approves what is released and unpaid.
--                             Any later change to it clears the approval.
--   Payment                   everything approved for one person, less what they owe back, is
--                             paid from a cash or bank account:
--                               debit   Commission payable
--                               credit  the cash or bank account
--
-- An accrual's figures (earned, released, paid) are always exactly the sum of its movements,
-- and a movement is never changed or removed: the database checks both.
--
-- Nothing of another step is changed. The hooks are triggers of this step's own on sales
-- documents (an invoice or a credit note is posted), on what receipts pay and on receipts (money
-- counts, stops counting, a cheque clears or bounces), and on what credit notes are set against.
-- Everything is written by the functions here; the app's role only reads, and calls
-- app.approve_commission and app.pay_commission.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE300 to SE399 (docs/PARALLEL.md); Step 37 used
-- SE301 to SE304:
--   SE310  no such commission in this company (or outside the member's branches)
--   SE311  nothing released and unpaid to approve, or nothing approved to pay
--   SE312  commission is approved and paid in read committed transactions
--   SE313  a date that has not come yet
--   SE314  commission is paid from a cash or a bank account that is in use
--   SE315  a commission movement is never changed or removed
--   SE316  an accrual is the sum of its movements
--   SE317  commission is paid by someone who works across the whole company
--   SE318  something is being recorded on one of the invoices right now; ask again
--   SE319  commission is paid on or after the day it was released

